{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require agencies and employers to pay umbrella and payroll processing fees",
        "additional_details": "I work as a self-employed subcontractor under CIS and am charged \u00a325 every week by a payment company just to receive money I have earned. Others I know are charged \u00a327.45 a week. That can mean over \u00a31,000 a year in compulsory payment-processing fees. Where an agency, hirer or employer requires a payroll, umbrella or payment company, the business should pay that cost, not the worker.",
        "background": "Change the law so workers, agency workers and Construction Industry Scheme (CIS) subcontractors cannot be charged fees just to receive their pay. I am charged \u00a325 a week. If an agency, hirer or employer requires a payroll or umbrella company, the business should pay the fee.",
        "closed_at": null,
